    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0364" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894A.00/6–2549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-25T13:00:00+08:00">June 25, 1949—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 25—4:01 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2490. Department might wish to consider some action re use of Taiwan as base for
                    blockading and bombing Shanghai. It occurs to me that action in this sense
                    perhaps in conjunction with other friendly powers in FEC<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d398-f1"/> might serve as basis for preventing Communist action
                    against Taiwan till Japanese treaty signed.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Canton 802.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d398-f1" n="80" xml:id="d398-f1-content">
